  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Text Mask Video\n\nAn animated gradient plays inside the letterforms, with a wipe reveal and a slow drifting pan and zoom.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A big title should be filled with moving footage or a flowing gradient instead of a flat colour.\n- A bold, short display word on a plain background.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The text is small or thin: the fill only reads inside heavy letterforms.\n- You need the text to stay legible over busy footage: use a caption block with an outline.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"MOTION\\nIN TYPE\"\n- font_size (number, 40-400): Font size, default 190\n- font_weight (number, 100-900): Font weight, default 900\n- line_height (number, 0.7-1.6): Line height, default 0.98\n- letter_spacing (number, -20-60): Letter spacing, default 0\n- color_1 (color): Gradient color 1, default \"#e8b86d\"\n- color_2 (color): Gradient color 2, default \"#f472b6\"\n- color_3 (color): Gradient color 3, default \"#2dd4bf\"\n- gradient_angle (number, 0-360): Gradient angle, default 115\n- reveal (enum): Reveal, default \"left\"\n- drift (number, 0-200): Drift, default 26\n- zoom (number, 0-0.6): Zoom, default 0.12\n- duration_frames (number, 4-120): Reveal duration, default 30\n- delay_frames (number, 0-120): Delay, default 6\n- exit (boolean): Exit, default false\n- font (enum): Font, default \"poppins\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Text Mask Video\n\n  An animated gradient inside the letterforms, with a wipe reveal.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui/blob/0aecaca2b61a167992e1205d10e4da16d8a71331/apps/web/registry/bases/default/primitives/text-mask-video.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 RemotionUI\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"text-mask-video\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"text\",\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"role\": \"content\",\n        \"label\": \"Text\",\n        \"description\": \"The text. A line break starts a new line.\",\n        \"default\": \"MOTION\\nIN TYPE\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font_size\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font size\",\n        \"description\": \"Text size in pixels.\",\n        \"default\": 190,\n        \"min\": 40,\n        \"max\": 400,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"px\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font_weight\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font weight\",\n        \"description\": \"Weight of the text (heavy reads best).\",\n        \"default\": 900,\n        \"min\": 100,\n        \"max\": 900,\n        \"step\": 100\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"line_height\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Line height\",\n        \"description\": \"Line height as a multiple of the font size.\",\n        \"default\": 0.98,\n        \"min\": 0.7,\n        \"max\": 1.6,\n        \"step\": 0.02\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"letter_spacing\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Letter spacing\",\n        \"description\": \"Extra spacing between letters, in pixels.\",\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"min\": -20,\n        \"max\": 60,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"px\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"color_1\",\n        \"type\": \"color\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Gradient color 1\",\n        \"description\": \"First colour of the fill gradient.\",\n        \"default\": \"#e8b86d\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"color_2\",\n        \"type\": \"color\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Gradient color 2\",\n        \"description\": \"Second colour of the fill gradient.\",\n        \"default\": \"#f472b6\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"color_3\",\n        \"type\": \"color\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Gradient color 3\",\n        \"description\": \"Third colour of the fill gradient.\",\n        \"default\": \"#2dd4bf\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"gradient_angle\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Gradient angle\",\n        \"description\": \"Angle of the fill gradient in degrees.\",\n        \"default\": 115,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 360,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"deg\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"reveal\",\n        \"type\": \"enum\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Reveal\",\n        \"description\": \"Direction of the wipe that reveals the fill.\",\n        \"default\": \"left\",\n        \"options\": [\n          {\n            \"value\": \"left\",\n            \"label\": \"Left to right\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"right\",\n            \"label\": \"Right to left\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"up\",\n            \"label\": \"Bottom to top\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"down\",\n            \"label\": \"Top to bottom\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"none\",\n            \"label\": \"None\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"drift\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Drift\",\n        \"description\": \"How far the fill pans behind the letters, in pixels.\",\n        \"default\": 26,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 200,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"px\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"zoom\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Zoom\",\n        \"description\": \"How much the fill breathes in scale.\",\n        \"default\": 0.12,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 0.6,\n        \"step\": 0.01\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"duration_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Reveal duration\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames (30 per second) the wipe takes.\",\n        \"default\": 30,\n        \"min\": 4,\n        \"max\": 120,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"delay_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Delay\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames before the wipe starts.\",\n        \"default\": 6,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 120,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"exit\",\n        \"type\": \"boolean\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Exit\",\n        \"description\": \"Unwind the wipe at the end of the clip.\",\n        \"default\": false\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font\",\n        \"type\": \"enum\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font\",\n        \"description\": \"Typeface.\",\n        \"default\": \"poppins\",\n        \"options\": [\n          {\n            \"value\": \"geist\",\n            \"label\": \"Geist\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"poppins\",\n            \"label\": \"Poppins\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"playfair\",\n            \"label\": \"Playfair Display\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"grotesk\",\n            \"label\": \"Space Grotesk\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Text Mask Video</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100..900&amp;family=Poppins:wght@400;600;800&amp;family=Playfair+Display:wght@400..900&amp;family=Space+Grotesk:wght@300..700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { color: #f4f4f5; }\n        .tmv-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .tmv-fill { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .tmv-fill > * { position: absolute; inset: -8%; width: 116%; height: 116%; object-fit: cover; }\n        .tmv-mask { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"text-mask-video\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"tmv-clip\" class=\"tmv-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <svg width=\"0\" height=\"0\" style=\"position:absolute\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><defs><clipPath id=\"tmv-shape\" clipPathUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\"></clipPath></defs></svg>\n          <div id=\"tmv-mask\" class=\"tmv-mask\"><div id=\"tmv-reveal\" class=\"tmv-fill\"><div id=\"tmv-pan\" class=\"tmv-fill\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\n            function num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) && v !== \"\" && v !== null ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\n            function str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\n            function bool(v, f) { if (v === undefined || v === null || v === \"\") return f; return !(v === false || v === \"false\" || v === 0 || v === \"0\"); }\n            function pick(v, list, f) { v = String(v); return list.indexOf(v) >= 0 ? v : f; }\n            function clamp01(v) { return v < 0 ? 0 : v > 1 ? 1 : v; }\n            function lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\n            function ramp(v, a, b, from, to, ease) { var p = b === a ? 1 : clamp01((v - a) / (b - a)); if (ease) p = ease(p); return from + (to - from) * p; }\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 30; i++) {\n                  var cx = 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * x1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                return 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * y1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            function mk(tag, parent, cls, text) { var e = document.createElement(tag); if (cls) e.className = cls; if (text !== undefined) e.textContent = text; if (parent) parent.appendChild(e); return e; }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"5\");\n            // Every frame is drawn from the frame number alone, so seeking anywhere draws the same frame.\n            function drive(name, frameFn) {\n              var clock = { f: 0 };\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { f: TOTAL * 30, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { frameFn(clock.f); } }, 0);\n              frameFn(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[name] = tl;\n            }\n\n            var FONTS = { geist: \"Geist, system-ui, sans-serif\", poppins: \"Poppins, system-ui, sans-serif\", playfair: '\"Playfair Display\", Georgia, serif', grotesk: '\"Space Grotesk\", system-ui, sans-serif' };\n            var fontKey = pick(vars.font, [\"geist\", \"poppins\", \"playfair\", \"grotesk\"], \"poppins\");\n            root.style.fontFamily = FONTS[fontKey];\n            var ARRIVE = bez(0.33, 1, 0.68, 1), ENTER = bez(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);\n            function EXIT(t) { return t * t * t; }\n            // Enter/exit contract of the source library's motion primitives: light leads the move (opacity done 55 % in), an exit is shorter and accelerates away.\n            function enterExit(frame, o) {\n              var et = clamp01((frame - o.delay) / o.duration);\n              var motion = ARRIVE(et), opacity = ENTER(clamp01(et / 0.55));\n              if (!o.exit) return { motion: motion, opacity: opacity, exiting: false, exitProgress: 0 };\n              var exitFrames = Math.max(6, Math.round(o.duration * 0.7));\n              var exitStart = Math.max(TOTAL * 30 - exitFrames, o.delay + o.duration);\n              var xt = clamp01((frame - exitStart) / exitFrames), xp = EXIT(xt);\n              var exiting = frame >= exitStart;\n              return { motion: exiting ? 1 - xp : motion, opacity: opacity * EXIT(1 - clamp01(xt / 0.7)), exiting: exiting, exitProgress: xp };\n            }\n\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"MOTION\\nIN TYPE\");\n            var lines = text.split(/\\r?\\n/);\n            var fontSize = num(vars.font_size, 190, 40, 400), weight = num(vars.font_weight, 900, 100, 900), lh = num(vars.line_height, 0.98, 0.7, 1.6), ls = num(vars.letter_spacing, 0, -20, 60);\n            var W = root.clientWidth || 1080, H = root.clientHeight || 1920, NS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            var clip = document.getElementById(\"tmv-shape\");\n            var blockH = (lines.length - 1) * fontSize * lh, firstY = H / 2 - blockH / 2;\n            var family = getComputedStyle(root).fontFamily;\n            lines.forEach(function (line, i) {\n              var t = document.createElementNS(NS, \"text\");\n              t.setAttribute(\"x\", String(W / 2)); t.setAttribute(\"y\", String(firstY + i * fontSize * lh));\n              t.setAttribute(\"text-anchor\", \"middle\"); t.setAttribute(\"dominant-baseline\", \"central\");\n              t.setAttribute(\"font-size\", String(fontSize)); t.setAttribute(\"font-weight\", String(weight)); t.setAttribute(\"letter-spacing\", String(ls));\n              t.setAttribute(\"font-family\", family);\n              t.textContent = line;\n              clip.appendChild(t);\n            });\n            var mask = document.getElementById(\"tmv-mask\"), revealEl = document.getElementById(\"tmv-reveal\"), pan = document.getElementById(\"tmv-pan\");\n            mask.style.clipPath = \"url(#tmv-shape)\"; mask.style.webkitClipPath = \"url(#tmv-shape)\";\n            mask.setAttribute(\"role\", \"img\"); mask.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n            // Fill: an animated gradient inside the letters.\n            var fillEl = mk(\"div\", pan);\n            var c1 = str(vars.color_1, \"#e8b86d\"), c2 = str(vars.color_2, \"#f472b6\"), c3 = str(vars.color_3, \"#2dd4bf\"), ang = num(vars.gradient_angle, 115, 0, 360);\n            fillEl.style.background = \"linear-gradient(\" + ang + \"deg, \" + c1 + \" 0%, \" + c2 + \" 25%, \" + c3 + \" 50%, \" + c2 + \" 75%, \" + c1 + \" 100%)\";\n            fillEl.style.backgroundSize = \"200% 200%\";\n            var reveal = pick(vars.reveal, [\"left\", \"right\", \"up\", \"down\", \"none\"], \"left\");\n            var drift = num(vars.drift, 26, 0, 200), zoom = num(vars.zoom, 0.12, 0, 0.6);\n            var o = { duration: num(vars.duration_frames, 30, 4, 120), delay: num(vars.delay_frames, 6, 0, 120), exit: bool(vars.exit, false) };\n            var INSET = { left: function (h) { return \"inset(0 \" + h + \"% 0 0)\"; }, right: function (h) { return \"inset(0 0 0 \" + h + \"%)\"; }, up: function (h) { return \"inset(0 0 \" + h + \"% 0)\"; }, down: function (h) { return \"inset(\" + h + \"% 0 0 0)\"; } };\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var s = enterExit(frame, o);\n              var revealed = reveal === \"none\" ? 1 : s.motion * (1 - (o.exit ? s.exitProgress : 0));\n              var hidden = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, (1 - revealed) * 100));\n              mask.style.opacity = String(s.opacity);\n              revealEl.style.clipPath = reveal === \"none\" ? \"\" : INSET[reveal](hidden.toFixed(2));\n              // Pan and zoom are sines, not ramps: a linear pan runs off the edge of a long shot.\n              var sec = frame / 30, px = Math.sin(sec * 0.62) * drift, sc = 1 + zoom * (0.5 + 0.5 * Math.sin(sec * 0.44 + 1.1));\n              pan.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + (-px).toFixed(2) + \"px) scale(\" + sc.toFixed(4) + \")\";\n              pan.firstChild.style.backgroundPosition = (50 + 50 * Math.sin(sec * 0.9)).toFixed(2) + \"% \" + (50 + 50 * Math.cos(sec * 0.7)).toFixed(2) + \"%\";\n            }\n            drive(\"text-mask-video\", draw);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
